Chapter: BlockSectorCount

 A disk is attached, so the count is the truth about it: 65536 bytes of
 fixture divided by 512 is 128 sectors. The sibling test block-identify
 attaches no disk and asserts 0, which is also true -- and which is why it
 could never see this bug. codex-vm served 0xFF on the LBA-mid and LBA-high
 ports, the floating-bus answer meaning "no drive", so the guest's ATA
 signature check bailed before it ever issued IDENTIFY and the count stayed
 at the 0 that emit-ata-init had written. The disk read perfectly the whole
 time. Only a test that attaches a disk and demands a specific number can
 tell a working counter from one that is stuck.

